/* Data packs for blocks/blend.html (prim:sound-spelling-blend): blend-en, blend-fr, blend-ja, blend-zh.
 *
 * Pack format
 *   units    { key: {say, cap, kind, ipa?, audio?} }  one sound box. `key` is the written glyph, optionally
 *            "glyph:variant" when the same glyph sounds different (ja "う:o" = う read as a long o,
 *            fr "t:0" = silent t). The box shows the part before ":". kind: c consonant | v vowel |
 *            silent | pause (ja っ) | long (ja ー) | ini / fin / tone (zh). `say` is what speech synthesis
 *            reads when the box is tapped: never a bare English/French phoneme (TTS cannot say one), but
 *            a keyword (en/fr), the mora itself (ja) or the 呼读音 / a character with that final (zh).
 *            `audio` (URL) overrides `say`: drop real recordings of the bare sound there.
 *            ja keys missing from `units` default to {say: glyph, kind: 'mora'}.
 *   words    [{id, text, boxes, gloss, pic, tag?, say?, py?, tricky?, pseudo?, audio?}]  regular words:
 *            boxes joined (glyph part) give `text` (zh: initial + final with the tone mark = `py`).
 *            `pseudo: true` = readable but not a word (used in 换一个音 and 听音摆字, never as a picture).
 *            `tricky` = index of the box hint 2 highlights.
 *   exceptions  same shape + {rule, actual}: words that do NOT decode by this pack's rule. Shown only in
 *            the 规则外 mode (reverse half), never as normal decoding items.
 *   chains   [[wordId, ...]]  each step changes, adds or removes exactly one box.
 *   foils    { key: [keys] }  distractor tiles for 听音摆字.
 */
